<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ferry capsizes and sinks off northern Cyprus, killing 8</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f771a9c31606f6a8cc1b6305735c5521d8c084eed730867584ace57da619e785</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:08:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus--feec88e2674e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus" /><summary type="html">At least eight people died when a ferry carrying more than 260 people capsized and sunk off the coast of northern Cyprus on Sunday, according to local authorities. The ship's captain and seven crew members were arrested, said the prime minister of the self-proclaimed Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (TRNC).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce93bb0676ca7f60d05c58c6f6b683669a1f8685de081588f2cdb7de10193104</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:30:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum--6c9761c1e20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum" /><summary type="html">Icelanders voted to reject reopening EU membership talks, official results showed Sunday, dealing a blow to the government's push to join the bloc and handing a win to those who argued the country's prized fishing waters were too important to risk. The results will disappoint Brussels, which had hoped to welcome the Nordic country as a new member.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman kills one at Swiss rave party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00053326d65d688f7d5a081839ea396034d305062d52618db70f3d90bee90f0d</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party--9d00787eff7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party" /><summary type="html">A large-scale police operation is underway in Switzerland after a shooting at a rave in the town of Aarau, 46 kilometres west of Zurich, left one person dead and five others injured. Swiss daily Blick reported that some attendees initially mistook the gunshots for fireworks, until someone shouted, “everyone down”. Police are appealing to potential witnesses who may have photos or videos of the incident to come forward and share them with investigators. France 24 correspondent John Zarocostas reports from Zurich.</summary></entry><entry><title>Manhunt under way after one killed, multiple injured at Swiss rave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daffbf08766c75ffb58c6750679af1a6294cd993db28c6c1e045d6d24be996ca</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:52:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland--affc514f1781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland" /><summary type="html">At least one person was killed and five others injured, some seriously, in a shooting at a rave in the northern Swiss city of Aarau, police and local media reported Sunday. A major police operation is underway at the scene, with authorities urging residents to stay away from the area.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Referendum on EU membership: An ‘existential question’ for Icelanders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d59ffd8737c4922045dbced5ff698eb960132a445841f4ee1ccccbd8ccd7a044</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders--be87b35411b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders" /><summary type="html">As Icelanders head to the polls on Saturday to vote in a referendum on whether the country should resume talks with the EU over membership, FRANCE 24 speaks to Eiríkur Bergmann, Professor of Politics at Bifröst University, for more insight into the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Warehouse hit by Russian attack stored munitions, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e2919de0c4e3aa47c6ac258563586350da0151d0f92099aa3fb0146cfde486</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:35:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says--67979b139afa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A depot that exploded in a Russian strike overnight was owned by the Ukrainian military and stored shells, drones, and other munitions, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Saturday. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dozens dead after Russian drone strike hits warehouse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8460d9fc3f9b6d52a732663a37700b5781822b21310485552d8ea190090bd0b7</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:24:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dozens-dead-after-russian-drone-strike-hits-warehouse--a049a730f3c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/dozens-dead-after-russian-drone-strike-hits-warehouse" /><summary type="html">At least 27 people have died after a Russian drone struck a depot near Kyiv's western suburbs overnight, sparking a huge fire and explosions, authorities said Saturday. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iceland votes on whether to resume EU membership negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99e127dcfbd1a173c41b6fb211de76b84f350a98ced63a6b11cbdf07662dfafc</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:57:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iceland-votes-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-negotiations--31c1b36cac9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iceland-votes-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-negotiations" /><summary type="html">Icelanders go to the polls on Saturday in a referendum on whether to resume membership negotiations with the European Union, in a tight race that will be closely watched in Brussels. The country of just under 400,000 people applied to join the EU in the wake of a 2009 financial crisis that devastated its economy. The membership talks were suspended in 2013 when a eurosceptic government came to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds evacuate after Russian strike on depot near Kyiv kills at least 37</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27d24bd8dac754938faa0483a0c2f5f13f15c1f8f810f2a83d4f0be52797cfef</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:57:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-russian-strike-on-warehouse-near-kyiv-kills-at-least-27-people-hundreds-evacuated--66e26e75e203.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-russian-strike-on-warehouse-near-kyiv-kills-at-least-27-people-hundreds-evacuated" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone strike on a depot on the outskirts of Ukraine's capital Kyiv on Friday killed at least 37 people and forced hundreds to evacuate, Ukrainian authorities said Saturday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes hit homes, warehouse, shopping mall across Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb8cc3ac1736d5a4f810f11b25c6750baef93386a235e6c69e4466f1668bd7b8</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-hit-homes-warehouse-shopping-mall-across-ukraine--c7e531cddf21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-hit-homes-warehouse-shopping-mall-across-ukraine" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone strike triggered a major fire and explosions at a warehouse on the outskirts of Ukraine's capital Kyiv, forcing hundreds to evacuate the region, authorities said early Saturday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Icelanders vote in tight referendum on restarting EU membership talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a66a4602185f27709d07a338566d91b5fdfe0f5a197151ede1600f879dcda2e3</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T06:56:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-icelanders-vote-in-referendum-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-talks--3f30a61fc087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-icelanders-vote-in-referendum-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-talks" /><summary type="html">Iceland will vote Saturday in a tight referendum on whether to reopen membership negotiations with the European Union. Reykjavik applied for EU membership in 2009, following a financial crisis that devastated its economy, but a eurosceptic government suspended the process in 2013.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Norway mourns King Harald as Haakon prepares to take the throne</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9e8b80818ed6c8c24f63bc7250ac266ba9fc3f762cafae1da6f5fb3c6167d0c</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:31:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/norway-mourns-king-harald-as-haakon-prepares-to-take-the-throne--82e23fa26c57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/norway-mourns-king-harald-as-haakon-prepares-to-take-the-throne" /><summary type="html">Norway is mourning King Harald V after the country's longest-serving monarch died at the age of 89, with tributes pouring in from across Europe. His death paves the way for Crown Prince Haakon to become king, as the royal family faces renewed scrutiny over Crown Princess Mette-Marit's reported past ties to Jeffrey Epstein and the conviction of her son for rape.</summary></entry><entry><title>Greenland to open truth commission over forced contraception scheme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:747a370f424ae541d6736d698eea1e1d6b4727c9631a7813fec41c0c15209e9c</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:05:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-greenland-to-open-truth-commission-over-forced-contraception-scheme--4b5e39560116.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-greenland-to-open-truth-commission-over-forced-contraception-scheme" /><summary type="html">Greenland's government said Friday it would ⁠establish a Truth and Reconciliation Commission to shed light on a campaign of forced contraception carried out by Danish authorities from the 1960s to 1990, after experts failed to agree on whether the practice constituted genocide. The brutal campaign saw thousands of Indignous women and girls receive intrauterine devices or contraceptive injections without their consent.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Austria: Anger over a business park being built on top of former Nazi camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9f7af21e26a48792e8e63e567ef02469e3db96241dcc1ee4992ee6eb09c286c</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T15:50:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/austria-anger-over-a-business-park-being-built-on-top-of-former-nazi-camp--5155736cbc28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/austria-anger-over-a-business-park-being-built-on-top-of-former-nazi-camp" /><summary type="html">Anger is growing in #Austria over the planned construction of a business park on top of what was a #Nazi concentration camp during the #SecondWorldWar. Around six million #Jewish people were murdered in the Holocaust, around half of them in concentration or extermination camps.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish government urges calm after Ceuta anti-migrant protesters clash with police</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:005ef9c945771ed5ad3c754cfd87a6c358d3cd2eb108d6ed8be1933836f41a79</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:44:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-spanish-government-urges-calm-anti-migrant-protesters-clash-police-ceuta--2f3295396100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-spanish-government-urges-calm-anti-migrant-protesters-clash-police-ceuta" /><summary type="html">Spain's left-wing government called for calm in the North African enclave of Ceuta on Friday after protests over security escalated into clashes between locals and police, a month after a mass influx of migrants from Morocco triggered a Europe-wide alert.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Rock en Seine: Visually impaired spectators enjoy festival with audio description</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b02fe681dbba260ba4903cc65546ccffb1ae5e3fb3a016be67e55d27f0071d0c</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T13:02:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rock-en-seine-visually-impaired-spectators-enjoy-festival-with-audio-description--3e90174085f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rock-en-seine-visually-impaired-spectators-enjoy-festival-with-audio-description" /><summary type="html">At Paris's Rock en Seine, visually impaired festival-goers can enjoy concerts through live audio description. The festival is offering dedicated platforms, as well as headphones and receivers provided by the Valentin Haüy Association, a pioneer in audio description in France. Spectators can experience a concert with audio description each day of the music festival, from August 26 to August 30.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbian war criminal Mladic to be buried with 'state honours'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40e94b67b05bdd3a008c5ef5d7dfd2b96f457730ebd159ec63ff3404738eb7be</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T11:40:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbian-war-criminal-mladic-to-be-buried-with-state-honours--b817391eb10c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbian-war-criminal-mladic-to-be-buried-with-state-honours" /><summary type="html">Convicted genocidaire Ratko Mladić has died at the age of 84 in a UN prison in The Hague, where he was serving a life sentence. He was found guilty of leading the siege of Sarajevo and orchestrating the 1995 Srebrenica massacre, in which more than 8,000 Bosniak men and boys were murdered. His planned burial with national honours has sparked sharp divisions in Serbia.</summary></entry><entry><title>EU wants Meta to extend US teen safety restrictions to Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25e757c21deaaca676fac4345a5de39951eccfe51f376ddd67fbffda71728801</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:13:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-wants-meta-to-extend-us-teen-safety-restrictions-to-europe--3d2aa02b5555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-wants-meta-to-extend-us-teen-safety-restrictions-to-europe" /><summary type="html">The EU is pressing Meta to introduce the same protections for under-18s in Europe that it agreed to in a landmark US settlement, including screen-time limits and stronger parental controls on Facebook and Instagram. Brussels is also demanding additional measures.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's Villena Treasure stolen in four-minute museum heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb1f0fdcdca205d20a90849600acb6b846202a236a439913b78959a100aebb1</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-villena-treasure-stolen-in-four-minute-museum-heist--6c51ba93267f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-villena-treasure-stolen-in-four-minute-museum-heist" /><summary type="html">Almost the entire Villena Treasure, one of Europe's most valuable Bronze Age collections, was stolen from a museum in eastern Spain in a four-minute raid after thieves smashed through a window and bulletproof glass. Police believe several people and vehicles were involved, and suspect the thieves created a diversion by triggering an alarm at a nearby sports centre before the break-in.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Harald's death puts focus on Norway's future king</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b707d76fc269874da37189c3c221ad93deffc1344d5d04385a321f0c2adf774</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:55:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/king-harald-s-death-puts-focus-on-norway-s-future-king--81286e650536.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/king-harald-s-death-puts-focus-on-norway-s-future-king" /><summary type="html">Following King Harald's death, attention is turning to Crown Prince Haakon, who is set to become Norway's next king after a turbulent year for the royal family. His wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit, underwent a lung transplant in June and has faced scrutiny over reported past ties to Jeffrey Epstein, while her son was sentenced to four years in prison for rape.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbian war criminal Ratko Mladic to be buried with 'state honours'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a1e1aaaadf59f4f49c4a893b7e6ea7e08ea0f5e97cd426154616d12d3b0c32f</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-serbian-war-criminal-ratko-mladic-to-be-buried-with-state-honours--d89ab53719eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-serbian-war-criminal-ratko-mladic-to-be-buried-with-state-honours" /><summary type="html">Former Bosnian Serb military leader Ratko Mladic, known as the “Butcher of Bosnia" for his role in the 1995 Srebrenica massacre, will be given a funeral with “military and state honours”, Serbian Justice Minister Nenad Vujic said Friday. Mladic died Thursday in The Hague where he was serving a life sentence for genocide, war crimes, and crimes against humanity.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Haakon VIII, the new face of a monarchy beset by woe and scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b473bd53e090882b99ff00ee0bfd433cbfdcc36bf6cca78cb30fedf3b0977ec</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T07:51:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-norway-s-king-haakon-the-new-face-of-a-monarchy-shaken-by-scandal--6a08812f415c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-norway-s-king-haakon-the-new-face-of-a-monarchy-shaken-by-scandal" /><summary type="html">Norway's King Haakon VIII automatically succeeded to the throne after his father, King Harald, passed away on Friday. He is the new face of a monarchy long praised for its modernity and modesty, but in recent years it has been beset by woe and scandal, including revelations about the queen's friendship with disgraced financier Jeffrey Epstein.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald V dies at 89, his son becomes King Haakon VIII</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70ac1b7d5654e68debde089ca0695a3685120e126bd7d0ea26fb95e519afae5</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T06:57:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-king-harald-v-of-norway-dies-at-89-and-his-son-becomes-king-haakon-viii--5224600ebd3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-king-harald-v-of-norway-dies-at-89-and-his-son-becomes-king-haakon-viii" /><summary type="html">King Harald V of Norway, who was Europe's oldest reigning monarch, died at the age of 89, the palace announced on Friday. He is automatically succeeded by his son, King Haakon VIII, the former crown prince.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kherson residents urged to leave as Russian attacks threaten power and heating</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab25889407b30411d89cf5b2348c217d153ed4fc3dfee0f6e3c09cc762619ec</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T22:40:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-kherson-residents-urged-to-leave-as-russian-attacks-threaten-power-and-heating--11be0f4eafa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-kherson-residents-urged-to-leave-as-russian-attacks-threaten-power-and-heating" /><summary type="html">Regional governor Oleksandr Prokudin urged residents to leave the southern Ukrainian city of Kherson on Thursday as Russian strikes damaged a district heating plant and threatened prolonged power and heating outages.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Former Bosnian Serb general Ratko Mladic convicted of genocide dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ac68192ffb0954faa23215f9cfe9cbcafc2add2c243f80de716ed88d8fd03b9</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:50:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-former-bosnian-serb-general-ratko-mladic-convicted-of-genocide-dies-state-media-says--7f145e326e9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-former-bosnian-serb-general-ratko-mladic-convicted-of-genocide-dies-state-media-says" /><summary type="html">Former Bosnian Serb military leader Ratko Mladic, convicted of genocide in the 1992-95 ​war ‌in Bosnia, has died in ​the United Nations detention centre in ​The ​Hague after suffering several strokes, according to local media.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Drought-hit Danube gives way to mammoth fossil hunt in Bulgaria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab280231c090ba26dd335fd19771b6e576a31db35d53c5a018e74d9be77b1dcf</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/drought-hit-danube-gives-way-to-mammoth-fossil-hunt-in-bulgaria--38d6967fd67d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/drought-hit-danube-gives-way-to-mammoth-fossil-hunt-in-bulgaria" /><summary type="html">As drought in Europe brings river levels to record lows, a group of volunteers scans the dried-up Danube riverbank in northern Bulgaria, not far from where the receding waters revealed mammoth bones in July. About 20 volunteers join an effort in the hope of discovering new fossils or artifacts in a search organised by the Regional Museum of History of Ruse.</summary></entry><entry><title>Game of Drones: Deep strikes into Russia keeping Ukraine 'in this game'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68224e83c72b8a63f5dc7f7e7f9bf54d2fdc64107582f0e253850e97b583239e</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T07:38:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/game-of-drones-deep-strikes-into-russia-keeping-ukraine-in-this-game--f722e007f6f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/game-of-drones-deep-strikes-into-russia-keeping-ukraine-in-this-game" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. He argues that Ukraine’s expanding long-range strike campaign has helped Ukraine “stay in this game” by raising the economic, military and social costs of Russia’s invasion and, crucially, by bringing the consequences of a distant war increasingly into Russian life. As Ukraine braces for another brutal winter with dangerously depleted air defenses, Kiev seeks to protect its own cities, civilians, and infrastructure.</summary></entry><entry><title>Man drives car into group of pedestrians in French city of Caen, killing two</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:572c889a1451aff391b1f516e8a5151278603be6fe3b26dfc80934fc2b9a0a9f</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T01:55:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-man-drives-car-into-group-of-pedestrians-in-french-city-of-caen-killing-one--24628e5dfae7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260827-man-drives-car-into-group-of-pedestrians-in-french-city-of-caen-killing-one" /><summary type="html">A car ploughed into pedestrians in the French city of Caen late Wednesday, killing two people and injuring nine others. Police detained a 26-year-old man after he fled the scene, while prosecutors said the incident was not currently being treated as terrorism.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'In Ceuta, they are eating the cats': Fake images and a persistent rumour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a16c5460977cb8ff554a2ffad4af02d5a03068d6bae84a6f6e3c3601624c3082</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T14:54:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ceuta-eating-cats-fake-images-persistent-rumour--7b799f8aab90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-eating-cats-fake-images-persistent-rumour" /><summary type="html">Cats “massacred” in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta? Three weeks after thousands of migrants crossed the border into Ceuta, Spanish websites and social media users are claiming that the migrants who have stayed are killing cats. But all of the dead cat photos that have been shared so far are either fake or have been taken out of context. Our team spoke to a local cat rescue organisation, which also confirmed that this is a rumour.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says CIA chief met Russian counterparts, not Putin, in Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:687598cb289bd0289e32b03f5428bea7f74abff025f8abd389dd144cf450344f</id><updated>2026-08-30T19:22:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T10:44:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260826-kremlin-says-cia-chief-met-russian-counterparts-not-putin-in-moscow--45b9e3b70f79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260826-kremlin-says-cia-chief-met-russian-counterparts-not-putin-in-moscow" /><summary type="html">CIA chief John Ratcliffe held ​talks with Russian intelligence officials during his visit to ​Moscow, ‌but did not ‌meet President Vladimir Putin, the Kremlin ⁠said Wednesday. President Donald Trump described Ratcliffe's visit to Moscow as a "semi-routine" mission, while implying that the intelligence chief was in the Russian capital to discuss the Ukraine war.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
